## Git Workflow

### Branches

```
main (production)
  └── develop (integration)
      ├── feature/* (new features)
      ├── fix/* (bug fixes)
      ├── refactor/* (refactoring)
      └── hotfix/* (urgent fixes)
```

### Naming Convention

- **Feature** : `feature/TICKET-description` (ex: `feature/ORDER-123-add-checkout`)
- **Fix** : `fix/TICKET-description` (ex: `fix/BUG-456-validation-error`)
- **Refactor** : `refactor/description` (ex: `refactor/optimize-queries`)
- **Hotfix** : `hotfix/vX.X.X-description` (ex: `hotfix/v1.2.1-security-patch`)

### Commits Convention

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

**Types** : feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore

**Examples** :
```bash
feat(order): add order creation endpoint
fix(validation): resolve email format issue
docs(readme): update installation instructions
refactor(repository): extract query builder logic
test(order): add CreateOrderHandler tests
```

**Reference** : `rules/09-git-workflow.md`

