## Golden Rules

### 1. Always Analyze Before Coding

NEVER start coding without having:
- Analyzed existing code
- Understood the need
- Designed the solution
- Planned the tests (TDD)

### 2. Respect the Architecture

- Clean Architecture layers
- Domain has NO external dependencies
- Dependency Inversion (interfaces in Domain)
- CQRS for use cases

### 3. Test Systematically

- Unit tests for all domain logic
- Integration tests for repositories
- Functional tests for endpoints
- Coverage > 80%

### 4. Mandatory Code Review

- No merge without approval
- Verify tests pass
- Verify code quality
- Verify documentation

### 5. Security First

- Input validation
- Parameterized queries
- Password hashing
- Secure secrets
- Regular audits

